  "description": "APPLICATION FOR (PHASE 2) VARIATION OF CONDITION 2 (APPROVED PLANS), ATTACHED TO LBM PLANNING APPLICATION 19/P1852 RELATING TO THE APPLICATION FOR APPROVAL OF RESERVED MATTERS (PHASE 2) FOLLOWING OUTLINE PERMISSION 17/P1721 FOR THE COMPREHENSIVE PHASED REGENERATION OF HIGH PATH ESTATE COMPRISING DEMOLITION OF ALL EXISTING BUILDINGS AND STRUCTURES; ERECTION OF NEW BUILDINGS RANGING FROM 1 TO 10 STOREYS MAX, PROVIDING UP TO 1570 RESIDENTIAL UNITS (C3 USE CLASS); PROVISION OF UP TO 9,900 SQM OF COMMERCIAL AND COMMUNITY FLOORSPACE (INC REPLACEMENT AND NEW FLOORSPACE, COMPRISING: UP TO 2,700 SQM OF USE CLASS A1 AND/OR A2, AND/OR A3 AND/OR A4 FLOORSPACE, UP TO 4,100 SQM OF USE CLASS B1 (OFFICE) FLOORSPACE, UP TO 1,250 SQM OF FLEXIBLE WORK UNITS (USE CLASS B1), UP TO 1,250 SQM OF USE CLASS D1 (COMMUNITY) FLOORSPACE; UP TO 600 SQM OF USE CLASS D2 (GYM) FLOORSPACE); PROVISION OF NEW NEIGHBOURHOOD PARK AND OTHER COMMUNAL AMENITY SPACES, INCL. CHILDREN'S PLAY SPACE; PUBLIC REALM, LANDSCAPING, LIGHTING; CYCLE PARKING (INCL VISITOR CYCLE PARKING) AND CAR PARKING (INC WITHIN GROUND LEVEL PODIUMS), ASSOCIATED HIGHWAYS AND UTILITIES WORKS. CHANGES RELATE TO AMENDMENTS TO PHASE 2B SO THAT IT COMPLIES WITH RECENTLY INTRODUCED FIRE SAFETY REGULATIONS INCLUDING, AMONG OTHER THINGS, A REQUIREMENT FOR TWO STAIRCASES PER CORE AND UPDATED BUILDING REGULATIONS PART L AND PART O RELATING TO ENERGY EFFICIENCY AND OVERHEATING. PHASE 2A RELATING TO THE DEMOLITION OF THE EXISTING BUILDINGS REMAINS UNCHANGED. ",
